# A manifest for looking at what makebelieve spends its time on. The outputs
# take noticeably different amounts of time to build, so they stand apart in a
# trace viewer, and the last rule serves the trace itself.
#
# The commands use `cmake -E`, so they work whether the shell is sh or cmd.exe.

@/fast.txt          = capture cmake -E echo "built quickly"
@/slow.txt          = run cmake -E sleep 1 && cmake -E echo "built slowly" > %out
@/copied.txt        = run cmake -E copy input.txt %out
@/nested/direct.txt = copy input.txt

# Everything makebelieve has done since the mount started, in the Trace Event
# Format. Open it in https://ui.perfetto.dev or chrome://tracing.
@/tracing.json = tracing
